    "title": "What Is an Impairment Rating?",
    "text": "quantifies the permanent loss of function from an injury, usually as a percentage. It differs from temporary restrictions and measures long-term deficits such as range-of-motion limitations, strength loss, sensory deficits, or chronic pain. IRs are commonly used in workers’ compensation, personal injury, and insurance claims and are typically calculated using standardized guides like the AMA Guides. Providers may include physical therapists, chiropractors, or physicians.\n\nWhat Is an Impairment Rating?"
